":"Find the middle angle","methodDirectNodeIds":{"fix-the-middle-angle":["cnm_h203","cnm_h020","cnm_271"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_h203","cnm_h020","cnm_271","cnm_h201","cnm_115","cnm_270"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C (8)","reason":"If the outer side is a, triangle ABD is equilateral, so BD=a and AC=√3a. For the similar inner rhombus, BD is the long diagonal, giving EF=a/√3. Its diagonal product, and therefore its area, is one third of the outer rhombus's: 24/3=8.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2006_AMC_12B_Q13","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_139","cnm_174","cnm_268"],"id":"diagonal-scale","label":"Corresponding diagonals and area scaling","methodDirectNodeIds":{"diagonal-scale":["cnm_189","cnm_270","math:similar-figure-area-scaling"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_189","cnm_270","math:similar-figure-area-scaling","cnm_139","cnm_174","cnm_268"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":5,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"C, 56","reason":"Triangles BDE and BAC are similar, so BD/AB=DE/AC. Since AB=AC, BD=DE. Therefore AD+DE=AD+BD=28, and the parallelogram perimeter is 2·28=56.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"2013_AMC_10A_Q12","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited","routes":[{"contextNodeIds":["cnm_055","cnm_069","cnm_270"],"id":"similar-triangles","label":"Method 2: Similar triangles","methodDirectNodeIds":{"similar-triangles":["cnm_183","cnm_271","cnm_272"]},"nodeIds":["cnm_183","cnm_271","cnm_272","cnm_055","cnm_069","cnm_270"]}]},{"additionalConceptCount":6,"answerCheck":{"derivedAnswer":"B: AO·AB","reason":"Since ∠AMB=∠AOP=90°, triangles AOP and AMB are similar. Thus AP/AB=AO/AM, giving AP·AM=AO·AB.","status":"matches"},"assessed":false,"bank":"amc","coverage":"canonical_concept_only","flags":[],"questionId":"1957_AMC_12_Q18","reviewStatus":"machine_scope_audited"